{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|codex|cōdex|lang=la}}, variant spelling of {{term|caudex||tree trunk”, “book”, “notebook|lang=la}}; compare {{term|caudex|lang=en}} (in botany).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{enPR|kōʹdĕks}}, {{IPA|/ˈkəʊdɛks/}},<ref name="OED">“[http://dictionary.oed.com/cgi/entry/50043046 codex]” listed in the '''Oxford English Dictionary''' [2<sup>nd</sup> Ed.; 1989]</ref> {{SAMPA|/"k@UdEks/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|codices|pl2=codexes}}

# an [[early]] [[manuscript]] [[book]]
# a book bound in the modern manner, by joining pages, as opposed to a rolled [[scroll]]
# an [[official]] [[list]] of [[medicine]]s and [[medicinal]] [[ingredient]]s

